cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AAAAG: frame-level ball possession from automatic tracking"
abstract: >-
  Team AAAAG's submission to More than a Hack 2027, Phase 1 (ball possession). A network
  trained only on other matches gives per-frame possession and dead-ball probabilities from
  automatic tracking, and a dead-gated semi-Markov decoder with controlled-possession rules turns
  them into possessions. Inference runs in numpy on a CPU and rebuilds the submitted file byte
  for byte.
